<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<graphml xmlns="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns/1.0/graphml.xsd">
  <key id="d6" for="edge" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d5" for="edge" attr.name="keywords" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d4" for="edge" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d3" for="edge" attr.name="weight" attr.type="double" />
  <key id="d2" for="node" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d1" for="node" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d0" for="node" attr.name="entity_type" attr.type="string" />
  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;SAINT-PIERRE-À-CHAMP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Saint-Pierre-à-Champ was a commune in France that existed until the late 19th century and was absorbed by the city of Paris. It had a significant population and was a center for trade and commerce in the region."&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0163</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VAL EN VIGNES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Val en Vignes is a commune in the Deux-Sèvres department of western France that absorbed Saint-Pierre-à-Champ in a recent merger."&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0163</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DEUX-SÈVRES DEPARTMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Deux-Sèvres department is a region in western France where Val en Vignes is located."&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0163</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FRENCH NATIONAL INSTITUTE FOR STATISTICS AND ECONOMIC STUDIES (INSEE)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"INSEE is a French national agency responsible for statistics and economic studies."&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0163</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FRENCH SENATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The French Senate is a legislative body in France that provides reports on various issues."&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0163</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PIERRE DUPONT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pierre Dupont is the mayor of Val en Vignes and spoke positively about the merger with Saint-Pierre-à-Champ."&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0163</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MARIE-FRANCE GARNIER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Marie-France Garnier is the former mayor of Saint-Pierre-à-Champ and expressed support for the merger."&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0163</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BARON HAUSSMANN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Baron Haussmann was a French urban planner who led the study recommending the annexation of Saint-Pierre-à-Champ by Paris."&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0163</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PARIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Paris is a city in France where AMP is located, known for its vibrant neighborhoods and rich history."&lt;SEP&gt;"Paris is the capital city of France and absorbed Saint-Pierre-à-Champ in the late 19th century."&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0163</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1870S&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The 1870s saw the beginning of urbanization projects in France, leading to the absorption of Saint-Pierre-à-Champ by Paris."&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0163</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1880&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"In 1880, Saint-Pierre-à-Champ was officially absorbed by Paris, marking the end of its existence as an independent commune."&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0163</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1875&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"In 1875, the French National Assembly passed a law authorizing the annexation of Saint-Pierre-à-Champ by Paris."&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0163</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1860S&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Studies conducted by the French Ministry of Urban Planning in the 1860s recommended the annexation of Saint-Pierre-à-Champ by Paris."&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0163</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;URBANIZATION PROJECTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Urbanization projects in the late 19th century aimed at modernizing France's infrastructure included the absorption of surrounding communes, such as Saint-Pierre-à-Champ, by Paris."&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0163</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;12TH CENTURY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Saint-Pierre-à-Champ was founded in the 12th century as a small agricultural village."&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0163</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;18TH CENTURY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"By the 18th century, Saint-Pierre-à-Champ had become a thriving town with a population of over 5,000 inhabitants."&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0163</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;19TH CENTURY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"In the late 19th century, Saint-Pierre-à-Champ was absorbed by Paris, marking a significant shift in the region's administrative landscape."&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0163</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RURAL COMMUNES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Rural communes are facing declining populations and increasing financial pressures, leading to mergers like the one between Saint-Pierre-à-Champ and Val en Vignes."&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0163</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MERGER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The merger between Saint-Pierre-à-Champ and Val en Vignes is part of a broader trend in France where rural communes are consolidating to improve administrative efficiency and sustainability."&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0163</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CONSOLIDATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Consolidation of rural communes is a strategy to streamline local governance and improve public services."&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0163</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AMP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"AMP is a thriving neighborhood in Paris, known for its current state and historical context."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0163</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FORMER COMMUNE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The former commune refers to a past political and social structure within AMP, highlighting a significant historical event."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0163</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;URBANIZATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Urbanization is a complex and contentious process that has shaped the history of both AMP and Paris."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0163</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FRANCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"France is the country where Paris and AMP are located, known for its diverse history and urban development."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0163</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COMPLEX AND CONTENTIOUS HISTORY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The complex and contentious history of urbanization in France reflects the challenges and debates surrounding urban development."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0163</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THRIVE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Thrive describes the current state of AMP, indicating its vitality and success."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0163</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VIBRANT NEIGHBORHOODS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Vibrant neighborhoods describe the current state of Paris, indicating its dynamic and lively areas."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0163</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INSEE&quot;">
      <data key="d2">cb-0163</data>
      <data key="d1">"Data from INSEE reveals that Saint-Pierre-à-Champ had a small population, making it one of the smallest communes in the region before the merger."</data>
      <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
    </node>
    <edge source="&quot;SAINT-PIERRE-À-CHAMP&quot;" target="&quot;VAL EN VIGNES&quot;">
      <data key="d3">10.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Saint-Pierre-à-Champ was absorbed by Val en Vignes in a recent merger, streamlining local governance and improving public services."</data>
      <data key="d5">"merger, governance improvement"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0163</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SAINT-PIERRE-À-CHAMP&quot;" target="&quot;DEUX-SÈVRES DEPARTMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Saint-Pierre-à-Champ was a commune in the Deux-Sèvres department before its merger with Val en Vignes."</data>
      <data key="d5">"administrative division"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0163</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SAINT-PIERRE-À-CHAMP&quot;" target="&quot;INSEE&quot;">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Data from INSEE reveals that Saint-Pierre-à-Champ had a small population, making it one of the smallest communes in the region before the merger."</data>
      <data key="d5">"population data, statistical analysis"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0163</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SAINT-PIERRE-À-CHAMP&quot;" target="&quot;FRENCH SENATE&quot;">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The French Senate reported that over 1,000 communes have merged since 2015, with many more expected to follow suit, including Saint-Pierre-à-Champ."</data>
      <data key="d5">"legislative report, trend analysis"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0163</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;VAL EN VIGNES&quot;" target="&quot;DEUX-SÈVRES DEPARTMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Val en Vignes is a commune in the Deux-Sèvres department after absorbing Saint-Pierre-à-Champ, serving as the primary governing entity for the area."</data>
      <data key="d5">"governing entity, administrative consolidation"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0163</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;VAL EN VIGNES&quot;" target="&quot;INSEE&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Val en Vignes, with a larger population, is better positioned to maintain its rural way of life while benefiting from economies of scale after the merger."</data>
      <data key="d5">"population comparison, resource management"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0163</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;VAL EN VIGNES&quot;" target="&quot;FRENCH SENATE&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Val en Vignes, as a result of the merger, is part of a broader trend in France where rural communes are consolidating to improve administrative efficiency and sustainability."</data>
      <data key="d5">"trend analysis, administrative reform"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0163</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;VAL EN VIGNES&quot;" target="&quot;PIERRE DUPONT&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Pierre Dupont, the mayor of Val en Vignes, welcomed the residents of Saint-Pierre-à-Champ and emphasized the benefits of the merger for the community."</data>
      <data key="d5">"community leadership, public statement"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0163</data>
    </edge>
